   "fen": "r1bqkb1r/2p2ppp/p1np1n2/1p2p1N1/3PP3/1B6/PPP2PPP/RNBQK2R b KQkq - 0 7",
   "line": [
    "Ng5",
    "d6",
    "d4"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 14,
   "t": 235.5,
   "fen": "r2qkb1r/2p2ppp/p1np1n2/1p2p1N1/3PP1b1/1B6/PPP2PPP/RNBQK2R w KQkq - 1 8",
   "line": [
    "Bg4"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 15,
   "t": 269.5,
   "fen": "r2qkb1r/2p2Bpp/p1np1n2/1p2p1N1/3PP1b1/8/PPP2PPP/RNBQK2R b KQkq - 0 8",
   "line": [
    "Bxf7+"
   ],
   "spoken": "The clean intermezzo is the bishop taking on f7 — a free pawn that drags the king into the open — rather than the knight capture, which would only trade queens.",
   "kind": "main",
   "teaches": [
    "Bxf7+: win a pawn and expose the king"
   ]
  },
  {
   "ply": 17,
   "t": 280.5,
   "fen": "r2q1b1r/2p1kBpp/p1np1n2/1p2p1N1/3PP1b1/5P2/PPP3PP/RNBQK2R b KQ - 0 9",
   "line": [
    "Ke7",
    "f3"
   ],
   "spoken": "We follow with f3, defending the queen with tempo and forcing the enemy bishop to declare itself.",
   "kind": "main"
  },
  {
   "ply": 18,
   "t": 287.5,
   "fen": "r2q1b1r/2p1kBpp/p1np1n2/1p2p1Nb/3PP3/5P2/PPP3PP/RNBQK2R w KQ - 1 10",
   "line": [
    "Bh5"
   ],
   "spoken": "Black's bishop to h5 actually helps us — our bishop was stranded on f7, and this hands us a free tempo to snap it off.",
   "kind": "main"
  },
  {
   "ply": 20,
   "t": 303,
   "fen": "r2q1b1r/2p1k1pp/p1np4/1p2p1Nn/3PP3/5P2/PPP3PP/RNBQK2R w KQ - 0 11",
   "line": [
    "Bxh5",
    "Nxh5"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 21,
   "t": 325,
   "fen": "r2q1b1r/2p1k1pp/p1np4/1p1Pp1Nn/4P3/5P2/PPP3PP/RNBQK2R b KQ - 0 11",
   "line": [
    "d5"
   ],
   "spoken": "Now we close the center with d5 — normally wrong with the enemy king exposed, but here for one concrete purpose: to plant a knight on e6, then reopen the position with f4 to even greater effect.",
   "kind": "plan",
   "teaches": [
    "a purposeful center-close to win the e6 outpost"
   ],
   "plans": [
    "Ne6 outpost, then f4 to reopen the f-file"
   ]
  },
  {
   "ply": 24,
   "t": 368.5,
   "fen": "rn3b1r/2pqk1pp/p2pN3/1p1Pp2n/4P3/5P2/PPP3PP/RNBQK2R w KQ - 3 13",
   "line": [
    "Qd7",
    "Ne6",
    "Nb8"
   ],
   "spoken": "The knight settles on e6 — an absolute monster of an outpost, right in the heart of Black's position.",
   "kind": "main",
   "teaches": [
    "the e6 knight outpost"
   ]
  },
  {
   "ply": 25,
   "t": 383,
   "fen": "rn3b1r/2pqk1pp/p2pN3/1p1Pp2n/4P3/5P2/PPP3PP/RNBQ1RK1 b - - 4 13",
   "line": [
    "O-O"
   ],
   "spoken": "We castle to prepare f4 methodically — the king gets safe and the rook is ready for the f-file that's about to open.",
   "kind": "main"
  },
  {
   "ply": 26,
   "t": 393,
   "fen": "rn3b1r/3qk1pp/p1ppN3/1p1Pp2n/4P3/5P2/PPP3PP/RNBQ1RK1 w - - 0 14",
   "line": [
    "c6"
   ],
   "spoken": "Black's c6 is no worry: the pawn on e4 defends d5, so a capture there doesn't win anything — it just opens the e-file for us.",
   "kind": "main",
   "teaches": [
    "the pawn chain holds; the capture only helps us"
   ]
  },
  {
   "ply": 27,
   "t": 408.5,
   "fen": "rn3b1r/3qk1pp/p1ppN3/1p1Pp2n/4PP2/8/PPP3PP/RNBQ1RK1 b - - 0 14",
   "line": [
    "f4"
   ],
   "spoken": "f4 reopens the center and pries open the f-file straight at the exposed king.",
   "kind": "main"
  },
  {
